import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { project, sourceUrl, verification } from '../data/project';
---
<Base title="Development" description="An evidence-backed snapshot of Scarp development: published alpha capabilities, limitations, source baseline, and next priorities.">
  <section class="wrap page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Current development state</p><h1>A clear view<br />of where we are.</h1><p class="lead">An experimental language, developed in public. Reviewed on 1 November 2026.</p></section>
  <section class="wrap status-summary"><div><span class="eyebrow">Published baseline</span><h2>v{project.version}</h2><p>Source modules · Experimental prerelease</p></div><div><a class="button primary" href={project.release}>Release notes ↗</a><a class="inline-link" href={verification}>Verification record ↗</a></div></section>
  <section class="wrap section prose"><h2>What you can use</h2><p>The published interpreter includes scalar values, typed functions and contracts, control flow, numerical vectors and tiles, relative source modules, explicit output streams, and execution budgets. Windows x64, Linux x64 GNU, and macOS ARM64 packages are published for this baseline.</p><h2>What “alpha” means</h2><p>Syntax, library APIs, diagnostics, and runtime behavior can change. Try small programs, keep the version with your examples, and report reproducible problems. A prerelease is not a stable compatibility promise.</p><h2>Known limitations</h2><ul><li>Programs are interpreted; there is no native-code generation command.</li><li>Source imports are bounded and relative. Runtime module globals and re-exports need further milestones.</li><li>General-purpose collections, user-defined types, a standard library, and a package manager are not available.</li><li>There is no general tensor engine, automatic differentiation, or GPU backend.</li><li>The interpreter reports the first error. Execution limits bound selected resources rather than total process RAM.</li><li><code>check</code> evaluates the selected program path without output. It is not a purely static type checker.</li></ul><h2>Next development priorities</h2><p>The source roadmap prioritizes module tooling, additional conformance, and source navigation, followed by constant-expression and library organization design. <a href="/roadmap/">Explore the longer path toward v1.0.0</a>.</p><h2 id="evidence">Evidence and freshness</h2><p>This website uses a reviewed snapshot. It makes no live claim about unmerged branches or unpublished work. The compiler repository and release record are authoritative when development moves ahead.</p><dl class="evidence-list"><dt>Published version</dt><dd><a href={project.release}>{project.tag}</a></dd><dt>Source commit</dt><dd><a class="mono" href={`${project.repo}/commit/${project.source}`}>{project.source}</a></dd><dt>Capability reference</dt><dd><a href={sourceUrl('README.md')}>Pinned compiler README ↗</a></dd><dt>Release verification</dt><dd><a href={verification}>Package and publication record ↗</a></dd><dt>Roadmap evidence</dt><dd><a href={sourceUrl('README.md') + '#prototype-limits-and-planned-roadmap'}>Pinned source roadmap ↗</a></dd><dt>Social links</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/scarp-lang/scarp-docs/blob/e38696bf97ba5b078f3a0802f0be9567aeec9d42/docs/community/social.md">Reviewed official account directory ↗</a></dd><dt>Machine-readable snapshot</dt><dd><a href="/project.json">project.json ↗</a></dd></dl></section>
</Base>
